Z||000000||Double07||10-03-2000||04:10 PM||||Just wondering, which V8 conversion kit is better?  The one from V8 Archie or the one from Pisa?    Which one gives you more for your money||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-03-2000||04:32 PM||||You forgot to include the Zumwalt kit.<P>I think its going to be your personal preference.<BR>Archie, I think, has more kits in use today so his expertise is valuable and he has probably solved most of the problems first time V8 engine swaps have encountered.  Archie hypes his product a lot and goes to a lot of Fiero shows.  His high visability and approachability makes him an easy choice.  Most all the kits are $2-3000 bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Double07||10-03-2000||05:46 PM||||Never heard of Zumwalt, where can i get info on them?  Also how is the Pisa kit||||reg||1
Z||000003||Richard Parnell||10-03-2000||06:18 PM||||As far as I know, the Zumwalt kit is not available any more.  I'm using the V8 Archie kit.  Being able to use stock axles on bothsides really makes me more comfortable as far as getting replacements quickly and cheaply. Install is not done yet.  Should be done next week.  I'll let you know after the test drive what I think.||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||10-04-2000||02:33 AM||||Pisa's kit is either zumalts kit or a copy of it. I would suggest Archies kit. He is/has been in business for a long time and can help you out when ever you need advise. I have used his 800 # a many of times for advise. Have always gotten great response.<P><BR>Scooter||||reg||1
